 | `workflow` | Execute YAML workflows |
 | `download <model>` | Download model from HuggingFace |
 
+## ARM64 / SBC (Orange Pi Zero 3W / Allwinner A733)
+
+whitt cross-compiles for `aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu`. The default build is CPU-only —
+no Vulkan headers required on host or target. See [`docs/cli-opi3w.md`](docs/cli-opi3w.md)
+for the full cheat sheet.
+
+### Build on x86_64 host
+
+```bash
+rustup target add aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu
+sudo apt install -y gcc-aarch64-linux-gnu g++-aarch64-linux-gnu
+cargo build --release --target aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu --features client
+```
+
+### Deploy + install on the SBC
+
+```bash
+scp target/aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu/release/whitt root@opi-zero3w.local:~/whitt
+scp scripts/install-opi3w.sh root@opi-zero3w.local:~/install-opi3w.sh
+scp configs/profiles/a733.yml    root@opi-zero3w.local:~/a733.yml
+
+ssh root@opi-zero3w.local
+chmod +x ~/install-opi3w.sh
+sudo ./install-opi3w.sh --binary ~/whitt
+sudo mkdir -p /etc/whitt && sudo mv ~/a733.yml /etc/whitt/config.yml
+```
+
+### Build llama.cpp natively on the SBC (CPU-only)
+
+```bash
+sudo apt install -y build-essential cmake git
+git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/ggerganov/llama.cpp
+cd llama.cpp
+cmake -B build -DLLAMA_CURL=ON -DLLAMA_OPENMP=ON -DLLAMA_NATIVE=OFF \
+  -DLLAMA_VULKAN=OFF -DLLAMA_CUDA=OFF -DLLAMA_METAL=OFF -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
+cmake --build build --config Release -j$(nproc)
+sudo cp build/bin/llama-server /usr/local/bin/
+```
+
+### Start llama-server + use whitt
+
+```bash
+# On the SBC
+llama-server -m /models/SmolLM3-3B-Q4_K_M.gguf -c 8192 -t 8 -ngl 0 \
+  --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080
+
+# In another terminal
+whitt --url http://127.0.0.1:8080 chat --model SmolLM3
+```
+
+### Docker on the SBC (optional)
+
+```bash
+docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.aarch64.yml up -d
+```
+
+### Helper CLI
+
+```bash
+whitt sbc info                          # deployment target summary (text/markdown/yaml)
+whitt sbc install --script              # generate pipeable bash deploy script
+whitt sbc install --script --from-ci-artifact   # download whitt from GitHub Actions
+whitt sbc doctor --host opi-zero3w.local # sanity checks via ssh (exit: 0=ok, 1=warn, 2=fail)
+whitt sbc doctor --json                 # machine-readable JSON
+```
+
+**Expected throughput** (CPU-only, 8 ARM cores, 12GB LPDDR5; rough estimate, NOT benchmarked):
+
+| Model | Quant | ~tok/s |
+|---|---|---|
+| SmolLM3 | Q4_K_M | 1–4 |
+| Qwen2.5-7B | Q4_K_M | 0.5–1.5 |
+| Qwen3.5-9B | Q4_K_M | 0.5–1.0 (tight on 12GB) |
+
